[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#problem-2-inconsistent-domain-models-across-services]

#### Problem 2: Inconsistent Domain Models Across Services

**Scenario**: Different interpretations of **\"Provider\"** concept across services.

**Provider in ValidationService**:

```csharp
// ValidationService - Minimal provider model
public class Provider
{
    public Guid ProviderId { get; set; }
    public string Npi { get; set; }
    public bool IsActive { get; set; }
}
```

**Provider in RulesEngineService**:

```csharp
// RulesEngineService - Provider with specialty
public class Provider
{
    public Guid ProviderId { get; set; }
    public string Npi { get; set; }
    public string SpecialtyCode { get; set; }
    public bool IsManagedCare { get; set; }
}
```

**Provider in WorkflowService**:

```csharp
// WorkflowService - Provider with credentialing status
public class Provider
{
    public Guid ProviderId { get; set; }
    public string Npi { get; set; }
    public string CredentialingStatus { get; set; }  // Pending, Approved, Suspended
    public DateTime CredentialExpirationDate { get; set; }
}
```

**Provider in ProviderDataService**:

```csharp
// ProviderDataService - Complete provider model
public class Provider
{
    public Guid ProviderId { get; set; }
    public string Npi { get; set; }
    public string TaxId { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public Address BusinessAddress { get; set; }
    public List<Specialty> Specialties { get; set; }  // 200+ properties total
    public bool IsActive { get; set; }
    // ... 195 more properties
}
```

**Problems**:

1. **No Ubiquitous Language**: \"Provider\" means different things in different services—no shared understanding
2. **Breaking Changes Cascade**: Adding `RequiresCredentialVerification` flag to Provider in RulesEngineService breaks ValidationService and WorkflowService
3. **Duplicate Logic**: Specialty validation logic duplicated in RulesEngineService and WorkflowService because they have different Provider models
4. **Database Coupling**: All services depend on ProviderDataService's database schema—any schema change affects all consumers
5. **Anemic Domain Models**: Provider is just a data structure—no behavior, no business rules, procedural logic scattered across services

**Impact Metrics**:

- **Provider Model Variants**: Multiple different Provider definitions across services
- **Breaking Changes**: Provider schema updates frequently break downstream services
- **Code Duplication**: Provider validation logic duplicated across multiple services
- **Integration Tests**: Provider model changes require regression testing across many services

