[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#1-entities-vs-value-objects]

#### 1. Entities vs. Value Objects

**Entity**: Object with unique identity that persists over time. Two entities with same data are still different if IDs differ.

```csharp
// Claims Bounded Context - Claim Entity
public class Claim : Entity<Guid>
{
    public Guid ClaimId { get; private set; }  // Identity
    public string ClaimNumber { get; private set; }
    public Guid ProviderId { get; private set; }
    public Guid MemberId { get; private set; }
    public ClaimStatus Status { get; private set; }
    public Money TotalAmount { get; private set; }
    public DateTime SubmittedAt { get; private set; }
    private List<ClaimLine> _claimLines;

    // Business behavior
    public Result Approve(Money approvedAmount, string adjusterId)
    {
        if (Status != ClaimStatus.Pending)
            return Result.Failure(\"Can only approve pending claims\");

        Status = ClaimStatus.Approved;
        TotalAmount = approvedAmount;

        // Raise domain event
        AddDomainEvent(new ClaimApprovedEvent(ClaimId, approvedAmount, adjusterId));

        return Result.Success();
    }
}
```

**Value Object**: Object without identity defined by its attributes. Two value objects with same data are identical.

```csharp
// Money Value Object - immutable, compared by value
public class Money : ValueObject
{
    public decimal Amount { get; }
    public string Currency { get; }

    public Money(decimal amount, string currency = \"USD\")
    {
        if (amount < 0)
            throw new ArgumentException(\"Amount cannot be negative\");

        Amount = amount;
        Currency = currency;
    }

    // Value objects are immutable—operations return new instances
    public Money Add(Money other)
    {
        if (Currency != other.Currency)
            throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Cannot add different currencies\");

        return new Money(Amount + other.Amount, Currency);
    }

    // Equality by value, not identity
    protected override IEnumerable<object> GetEqualityComponents()
    {
        yield return Amount;
        yield return Currency;
    }
}
```

**Guidelines**:

- Use **Entities** for: Claim, Provider, Member, Payment (tracked over time with unique ID)
- Use **Value Objects** for: Money, Address, DateRange, DiagnosisCode (no identity, compared by value)

