[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#2-aggregates-consistency-boundaries]

#### 2. Aggregates: Consistency Boundaries

An **aggregate** is a cluster of entities and value objects with a single **aggregate root** that enforces consistency rules.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Claim Aggregate"
        ClaimRoot[Claim<br/>Aggregate Root]
        ClaimLine1[ClaimLine Entity]
        ClaimLine2[ClaimLine Entity]
        Payment[Payment<br/>Value Object]
        Diagnosis[Diagnosis Code<br/>Value Object]

        ClaimRoot -->|Owns| ClaimLine1
        ClaimRoot -->|Owns| ClaimLine2
        ClaimRoot -->|Has| Payment
        ClaimRoot -->|Has| Diagnosis
    end

    ExternalService[External Service] -->|Only accesses through<br/>aggregate root| ClaimRoot
    ExternalService -.->|❌ Cannot directly<br/>modify| ClaimLine1

    style ClaimRoot fill:#FFD700
    style ClaimLine1 fill:#e1f5ff
    style ClaimLine2 fill:#e1f5ff
```

**Aggregate Rules**:

1. **External references only through aggregate root**: Cannot directly access ClaimLine—must go through Claim
2. **Consistency boundary**: All invariants enforced by aggregate root
3. **Transaction boundary**: Save entire aggregate in single transaction
4. **Small aggregates**: Keep aggregates small—don't include entire Provider in Claim aggregate

**Implementation**:

```csharp
// Claim Aggregate Root
public class Claim : AggregateRoot<Guid>
{
    private List<ClaimLine> _claimLines = new List<ClaimLine>();
    public IReadOnlyList<ClaimLine> ClaimLines => _claimLines.AsReadOnly();

    // ✅ Add claim line through aggregate root
    public Result AddClaimLine(ClaimLine claimLine)
    {
        // Enforce invariant: No duplicate service codes on same date
        if (_claimLines.Any(cl =>
            cl.ServiceCode == claimLine.ServiceCode &&
            cl.ServiceDate == claimLine.ServiceDate))
        {
            return Result.Failure(\"Duplicate service on same date\");
        }

        // Enforce invariant: Total claim lines cannot exceed claim limit
        var newTotal = _claimLines.Sum(cl => cl.Amount) + claimLine.Amount;
        if (newTotal > GetMaxClaimAmount())
        {
            return Result.Failure(\"Exceeds maximum claim amount\");
        }

        _claimLines.Add(claimLine);
        return Result.Success();
    }

    // ClaimLine cannot exist without Claim—not a separate aggregate
}

// ClaimLine Entity (NOT an aggregate root)
public class ClaimLine : Entity<Guid>
{
    public Guid ClaimLineId { get; private set; }
    public string ServiceCode { get; private set; }
    public DateTime ServiceDate { get; private set; }
    public Money Amount { get; private set; }

    // No public constructor—only Claim can create ClaimLines
    internal ClaimLine(string serviceCode, DateTime serviceDate, Money amount)
    {
        ClaimLineId = Guid.NewGuid();
        ServiceCode = serviceCode;
        ServiceDate = serviceDate;
        Amount = amount;
    }
}
```

