[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#3-domain-events-business-significant-state-changes]

#### 3. Domain Events: Business-Significant State Changes

**Domain events** represent business-significant occurrences within a bounded context.

```csharp
// Domain Event - immutable record of what happened
public class ClaimApprovedEvent : DomainEvent
{
    public Guid ClaimId { get; }
    public Money ApprovedAmount { get; }
    public string AdjusterId { get; }
    public DateTime ApprovedAt { get; }

    public ClaimApprovedEvent(Guid claimId, Money approvedAmount, string adjusterId)
    {
        ClaimId = claimId;
        ApprovedAmount = approvedAmount;
        AdjusterId = adjusterId;
        ApprovedAt = DateTime.UtcNow;
    }
}

// Aggregate raises domain events
public class Claim : AggregateRoot<Guid>
{
    public Result Approve(Money approvedAmount, string adjusterId)
    {
        // Business logic
        Status = ClaimStatus.Approved;
        TotalAmount = approvedAmount;

        // Raise domain event for other bounded contexts
        AddDomainEvent(new ClaimApprovedEvent(ClaimId, approvedAmount, adjusterId));

        return Result.Success();
    }
}

// Event handler in Provider context updates provider statistics
public class ClaimApprovedEventHandler : IDomainEventHandler<ClaimApprovedEvent>
{
    private readonly IProviderRepository _providerRepo;

    public async Task HandleAsync(ClaimApprovedEvent evt)
    {
        var provider = await _providerRepo.GetByClaimProviderIdAsync(evt.ClaimId);
        provider.UpdateClaimStatistics(evt.ApprovedAmount);
        await _providerRepo.SaveAsync(provider);
    }
}
```

**Domain Events vs. Integration Events**:

- **Domain Events**: Within bounded context, in-process, transactional (ClaimApprovedEvent handled by Provider statistics updater)
- **Integration Events**: Across bounded contexts, asynchronous, eventual consistency (ClaimApprovedIntegrationEvent published to Azure Service Bus for Analytics Service)

