[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#4-repositories-domain-driven-data-access]

#### 4. Repositories: Domain-Driven Data Access

**Repository** abstracts data persistence using domain language, not database terminology.

```csharp
// Repository interface in domain layer (no database details)
public interface IClaimRepository
{
    // Domain language, not SQL
    Task<Claim> GetByClaimNumberAsync(string claimNumber);
    Task<IEnumerable<Claim>> GetPendingClaimsForProviderAsync(Guid providerId);
    Task SaveAsync(Claim claim);

    // ❌ Avoid: GetByIdAsync(Guid id) - too technical
    // ✅ Better: GetByClaimNumberAsync(string claimNumber) - domain language
}

// Repository implementation in infrastructure layer
public class ClaimRepository : IClaimRepository
{
    private readonly ClaimsDbContext _dbContext;

    public async Task<Claim> GetByClaimNumberAsync(string claimNumber)
    {
        // Load aggregate with all child entities
        return await _dbContext.Claims
            .Include(c => c.ClaimLines)
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(c => c.ClaimNumber == claimNumber);
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Claim claim)
    {
        // Save entire aggregate
        if (_dbContext.Entry(claim).State == EntityState.Detached)
            _dbContext.Claims.Add(claim);

        await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();

        // Publish domain events after persistence
        await PublishDomainEventsAsync(claim);
    }
}
```

