[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#pattern-1-api-based-integration-customer-supplier]

#### Pattern 1: API-Based Integration (Customer-Supplier)

Claims Service (customer) calls Provider Service (supplier) API:

```csharp
// Claims Bounded Context - Anti-Corruption Layer
public class ProviderAntiCorruptionLayer
{
    private readonly IProviderServiceClient _providerClient;

    // Translate Provider Service API model to Claims domain model
    public async Task<ClaimsProviderInfo> GetProviderForClaimAsync(Guid providerId)
    {
        // Call Provider Service API
        var providerDto = await _providerClient.GetProviderAsync(providerId);

        // Translate to Claims domain model (only what Claims needs)
        return new ClaimsProviderInfo(
            providerId: providerDto.ProviderId,
            npi: providerDto.Npi,
            isActive: providerDto.Status == \"Active\",
            specialtyCode: providerDto.PrimarySpecialtyCode
        );
        // Ignore 200+ other Provider fields—Claims doesn't care
    }
}

// Claims domain model - simplified Provider concept
public class ClaimsProviderInfo : ValueObject
{
    public Guid ProviderId { get; }
    public string Npi { get; }
    public bool IsActive { get; }
    public string SpecialtyCode { get; }

    // Claims-specific provider validation
    public bool IsEligibleForServiceCode(string serviceCode)
    {
        // Claims domain logic, not Provider domain logic
        return IsActive && ServiceCodeMatchesSpecialty(serviceCode, SpecialtyCode);
    }
}
```

