[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#pattern-2-event-driven-integration-publisher-subscriber]

#### Pattern 2: Event-Driven Integration (Publisher-Subscriber)

Provider Service publishes events, Claims Service subscribes:

```csharp
// Provider Bounded Context - Publishes integration event
public class Provider : AggregateRoot<Guid>
{
    public Result Suspend(string reason)
    {
        Status = ProviderStatus.Suspended;

        // Raise integration event for other bounded contexts
        AddIntegrationEvent(new ProviderSuspendedIntegrationEvent
        {
            ProviderId = ProviderId,
            Npi = Npi,
            SuspendedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
            Reason = reason
        });

        return Result.Success();
    }
}

// Claims Bounded Context - Handles integration event
public class ProviderSuspendedIntegrationEventHandler
    : IIntegrationEventHandler<ProviderSuspendedIntegrationEvent>
{
    private readonly IClaimRepository _claimRepo;

    public async Task HandleAsync(ProviderSuspendedIntegrationEvent evt)
    {
        // Update Claims context's view of provider
        // (Don't directly access Provider database)
        var pendingClaims = await _claimRepo
            .GetPendingClaimsForProviderAsync(evt.ProviderId);

        foreach (var claim in pendingClaims)
        {
            claim.SuspendDueToProviderIssue(evt.Reason);
        }

        await _claimRepo.SaveManyAsync(pendingClaims);
    }
}
```

page_texts.30:
[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-008-domain-driven-design-pattern.md#pattern-3-shared-kernel-tight-coupling-accepted]

#### Pattern 3: Shared Kernel (Tight Coupling Accepted)

Claims and Payment share Payment domain model:

```csharp
// Shared Kernel - Payment domain model shared by Claims and Payment contexts
namespace Gainwell.SharedKernel.Payment
{
    public class PaymentTransaction : Entity<Guid>
    {
        public Guid PaymentId { get; private set; }
        public Guid ClaimId { get; private set; }
        public Money Amount { get; private set; }
        public PaymentMethod Method { get; private set; }
        public PaymentStatus Status { get; private set; }

        // Shared business rules
        public Result Process()
        {
            if (Status != PaymentStatus.Pending)
                return Result.Failure(\"Payment already processed\");

            Status = PaymentStatus.Processing;
            return Result.Success();
        }
    }
}

// Both Claims and Payment contexts use shared kernel
// Tight coupling accepted because payment is transactionally tied to claims
```

