### Example 1: Claims Processing Bounded Context - Full Implementation

This example demonstrates a complete bounded context implementation for claims processing, showing how DDD patterns transform a technical service architecture into a business-aligned domain model.

**Business Context:**

Gainwell's Claims Processing handles 500,000+ medical claims daily across 50+ state Medicaid programs. Each claim must be validated, priced according to state-specific fee schedules, adjudicated against 200+ business rules, and approved or denied for payment.

**Before DDD (Technical Decomposition):**

```csharp
// Legacy approach - scattered business logic across technical services

// ClaimsDataService (Data Access Layer)
public class ClaimsDataService
{
    public async Task<ClaimEntity> GetClaimByIdAsync(Guid claimId)
    {
        return await _dbContext.Claims.FindAsync(claimId);
    }

    public async Task UpdateClaimAsync(ClaimEntity claim)
    {
        _dbContext.Claims.Update(claim);
        await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}

// ValidationService (Business Logic Layer)
public class ValidationService
{
    public async Task<ValidationResult> ValidateClaimAsync(Guid claimId)
    {
        var claim = await _claimsDataService.GetClaimByIdAsync(claimId);
        var provider = await _providerDataService.GetProviderByIdAsync(claim.ProviderId);
        var member = await _memberDataService.GetMemberByIdAsync(claim.MemberId);

        // Validation logic scattered here
        if (provider == null || !provider.IsActive)
            return ValidationResult.Failed("Provider not active");

        if (member == null || member.EnrollmentStatus != "Active")
            return ValidationResult.Failed("Member not eligible");

        return ValidationResult.Success();
    }
}

// RulesEngineService (Business Logic Layer)
public class RulesEngineService
{
    public async Task<AdjudicationResult> AdjudicateClaimAsync(Guid claimId)
    {
        var claim = await _claimsDataService.GetClaimByIdAsync(claimId);

        // Load 200+ rules from database
        var rules = await _rulesDataService.GetRulesForStateAsync(claim.StateCode);

        // Execute rules (business logic scattered here)
        foreach (var rule in rules)
        {
            var ruleResult = await ExecuteRuleAsync(rule, claim);
            if (!ruleResult.Passed)
                return AdjudicationResult.Denied(ruleResult.Reason);
        }

        return AdjudicationResult.Approved(calculatedAmount);
    }
}

// ClaimsController (Presentation Layer)
public class ClaimsController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpPost("api/claims")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitClaim([FromBody] ClaimRequest request)
    {
        // Orchestration logic in controller
        var claimEntity = _mapper.Map<ClaimEntity>(request);
        await _claimsDataService.CreateClaimAsync(claimEntity);

        var validationResult = await _validationService.ValidateClaimAsync(claimEntity.Id);
        if (!validationResult.IsValid)
            return BadRequest(validationResult.Errors);

        var pricingResult = await _pricingService.PriceClaimAsync(claimEntity.Id);
        var adjudicationResult = await _rulesEngineService.AdjudicateClaimAsync(claimEntity.Id);

        if (adjudicationResult.IsApproved)
        {
            claimEntity.Status = "Approved";
            claimEntity.ApprovedAmount = adjudicationResult.Amount;
            await _claimsDataService.UpdateClaimAsync(claimEntity);
        }

        return Ok(new { claimId = claimEntity.Id, status = claimEntity.Status });
    }
}

// Problems:
// - Business logic scattered across 5 services
// - No clear ownership (Claims team? Validation team? Rules team?)
// - Anemic domain model (ClaimEntity is just properties, no behavior)
// - Tight coupling (controller knows about 4+ services)
// - 7 database round-trips per claim submission
// - Difficult to test (need to mock 5 services)
// - No ubiquitous language (technical terms like "Entity", "Service")
```

**Measured Impact of Legacy Approach:**

| Metric | Value | Issue |
|--------|-------|-------|
| **Services Modified per Change** | Multiple services | Business rule change requires touching ValidationService, RulesEngineService, and ClaimsDataService |
| **Deployment Coordination** | 5 weeks | All 3 services must deploy together (tight coupling) |
| **Change Failure Rate** | Elevated | Logic scattered across services causes integration bugs |
| **Mean Time to Recovery** | Hours | Hard to isolate which service caused failure |
| **Developer Cognitive Load** | High | Developers must understand 5+ services to implement one feature |
| **Test Execution Time** | Extended | Integration tests require all services running |

**After DDD (Bounded Context):**

```csharp
// Claims Processing Bounded Context - Domain Model

// 1. AGGREGATES - Encapsulate business logic and enforce invariants

public class Claim : AggregateRoot<ClaimId>
{
    private readonly List<ClaimLine> _claimLines = new();

    // Domain properties (ubiquitous language)
    public ClaimNumber ClaimNumber { get; private set; }
    public ProviderId ProviderId { get; private set; }
    public MemberId MemberId { get; private set; }
    public DateOfService ServiceDate { get; private set; }
    public ClaimStatus Status { get; private set; }
    public Money TotalBilledAmount { get; private set; }
    public Money TotalAllowedAmount { get; private set; }
    public DenialReason? DenialReason { get; private set; }

    public IReadOnlyList<ClaimLine> ClaimLines => _claimLines.AsReadOnly();

    // Factory method (replaces anemic constructor)
    public static Claim Submit(
        ClaimNumber claimNumber,
        ProviderId providerId,
        MemberId memberId,
        DateOfService serviceDate,
        List<ClaimLineData> lines)
    {
        // Business rules enforced at creation
        if (!lines.Any())
            throw new DomainException("Claim must have at least one service line");

        if (serviceDate.IsInFuture())
            throw new DomainException("Cannot submit claim for future service date");

        var claim = new Claim
        {
            Id = ClaimId.New(),
            ClaimNumber = claimNumber,
            ProviderId = providerId,
            MemberId = memberId,
            ServiceDate = serviceDate,
            Status = ClaimStatus.Submitted
        };

        foreach (var lineData in lines)
        {
            claim.AddClaimLine(
                lineData.ServiceCode,
                lineData.Units,
                lineData.ChargedAmount,
                lineData.DiagnosisCodes);
        }

        // Domain event (not integration event)
        claim.AddDomainEvent(new ClaimSubmittedEvent(
            claim.Id,
            claim.ClaimNumber,
            claim.TotalBilledAmount));

        return claim;
    }

    // Business behavior (replaces scattered service calls)
    public AdjudicationResult Adjudicate(
        MemberEligibility eligibility,
        ProviderCredential credential,
        FeeSchedule pricing,
        PriorAuthorizationPolicy authPolicy)
    {
        // Invariant: Can only adjudicate submitted claims
        if (Status != ClaimStatus.Submitted)
            throw new DomainException($"Cannot adjudicate claim in {Status} status");

        // Business Rule 1: Member must be eligible
        if (!eligibility.IsActiveOn(ServiceDate))
        {
            Deny(DenialReason.MemberNotEligible);
            return AdjudicationResult.Denied(DenialReason.MemberNotEligible);
        }

        // Business Rule 2: Provider must be credentialed
        if (!credential.IsValidOn(ServiceDate))
        {
            Deny(DenialReason.ProviderNotCredentialed);
            return AdjudicationResult.Denied(DenialReason.ProviderNotCredentialed);
        }

        // Business Rule 3: Prior authorization required for certain services
        var lineResults = new List<ClaimLineAdjudication>();
        foreach (var line in _claimLines)
        {
            if (authPolicy.RequiresAuthorization(line.ServiceCode))
            {
                var auth = authPolicy.GetAuthorization(line.ServiceCode, ServiceDate);
                if (auth == null || auth.IsExpired)
                {
                    line.Deny(DenialReason.AuthorizationRequired);
                    continue;
                }
            }

            // Business Rule 4: Apply state-specific pricing
            var allowedAmount = pricing.GetAllowedAmount(
                line.ServiceCode,
                line.Units,
                credential.SpecialtyCode);

            line.Approve(allowedAmount);
            lineResults.Add(new ClaimLineAdjudication(line.Id, allowedAmount));
        }

        // Calculate totals (business logic)
        TotalAllowedAmount = _claimLines
            .Where(l => l.Status == ClaimLineStatus.Approved)
            .Aggregate(Money.Zero, (sum, line) => sum.Add(line.AllowedAmount));

        // Update claim status based on line results
        if (_claimLines.All(l => l.Status == ClaimLineStatus.Approved))
        {
            Status = ClaimStatus.Approved;
            AddDomainEvent(new ClaimApprovedEvent(Id, ClaimNumber, TotalAllowedAmount));
        }
        else if (_claimLines.All(l => l.Status == ClaimLineStatus.Denied))
        {
            Status = ClaimStatus.Denied;
            DenialReason = _claimLines.First().DenialReason;
            AddDomainEvent(new ClaimDeniedEvent(Id, ClaimNumber, DenialReason.Value));
        }
        else
        {
            Status = ClaimStatus.PartiallyApproved;
            AddDomainEvent(new ClaimPartiallyApprovedEvent(Id, ClaimNumber, TotalAllowedAmount));
        }

        return new AdjudicationResult(Status, lineResults);
    }

    private void Deny(DenialReason reason)
    {
        Status = ClaimStatus.Denied;
        DenialReason = reason;
        AddDomainEvent(new ClaimDeniedEvent(Id, ClaimNumber, reason));
    }

    // Invariant enforcement
    private void AddClaimLine(
        ServiceCode serviceCode,
        int units,
        Money chargedAmount,
        List<DiagnosisCode> diagnosisCodes)
    {
        // Invariant: No duplicate service codes
        if (_claimLines.Any(l => l.ServiceCode == serviceCode))
            throw new DomainException($"Duplicate service code {serviceCode}");

        // Invariant: Total claim amount cannot exceed state limit
        var newTotal = TotalBilledAmount.Add(chargedAmount);
        if (newTotal.IsGreaterThan(Money.FromDollars(50000)))
            throw new DomainException("Claim amount exceeds state limit of $50,000");

        // Invariant: At least one diagnosis code required
        if (!diagnosisCodes.Any())
            throw new DomainException("Claim line must have at least one diagnosis code");

        var line = ClaimLine.Create(ClaimLineId.New(), Id, serviceCode, units, chargedAmount, diagnosisCodes);
        _claimLines.Add(line);
        TotalBilledAmount = TotalBilledAmount.Add(chargedAmount);
    }
}

// 2. VALUE OBJECTS - Immutable domain concepts

public record Money
{
    public decimal Amount { get; init; }
    public string Currency { get; init; }

    public static Money FromDollars(decimal amount)
    {
        if (amount < 0)
            throw new DomainException("Amount cannot be negative");
        return new Money { Amount = amount, Currency = "USD" };
    }

    public static Money Zero => new() { Amount = 0, Currency = "USD" };

    public Money Add(Money other)
    {
        if (Currency != other.Currency)
            throw new DomainException("Cannot add different currencies");
        return FromDollars(Amount + other.Amount);
    }

    public bool IsGreaterThan(Money other) => Amount > other.Amount;
}

public record ClaimNumber
{
    public string Value { get; init; }

    public static ClaimNumber Create(string stateCode, int year, long sequence)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(stateCode) || stateCode.Length != 2)
            throw new DomainException("Invalid state code");

        return new ClaimNumber
        {
            Value = $"{stateCode.ToUpper()}-{year}-{sequence:D10}"
        };
    }
}

// 3. APPLICATION SERVICE - Orchestrates domain model

public class ClaimApplicationService : IClaimApplicationService
{
    private readonly IClaimRepository _claimRepo;
    private readonly IProviderClient _providerClient; // Anti-Corruption Layer
    private readonly IMemberClient _memberClient;     // Anti-Corruption Layer
    private readonly IFeeScheduleRepository _feeScheduleRepo;
    private readonly IPriorAuthorizationPolicy _authPolicy;

    public async Task<Result<ClaimSubmissionResult>> SubmitClaimAsync(SubmitClaimCommand command)
    {
        // Validate provider (ACL translates Provider context model to Claims model)
        var provider = await _providerClient.GetProviderAsync(command.ProviderId);
        if (provider == null || !provider.IsActive)
            return Result.Failure<ClaimSubmissionResult>("Provider not active");

        // Validate member eligibility (ACL translates Member context model)
        var member = await _memberClient.GetMemberAsync(command.MemberId);
        if (!member.IsEligibleOn(command.ServiceDate))
            return Result.Failure<ClaimSubmissionResult>("Member not eligible");

        // Create Claim aggregate (business logic encapsulated in domain model)
        var claim = Claim.Submit(
            ClaimNumber.Create(command.StateCode, DateTime.UtcNow.Year, GenerateSequence()),
            ProviderId.From(command.ProviderId),
            MemberId.From(command.MemberId),
            DateOfService.FromDate(command.ServiceDate),
            command.ClaimLines.Select(l => new ClaimLineData
            {
                ServiceCode = ServiceCode.FromCpt(l.ServiceCode),
                Units = l.Units,
                ChargedAmount = Money.FromDollars(l.ChargedAmount),
                DiagnosisCodes = l.DiagnosisCodes.Select(DiagnosisCode.FromIcd10).ToList()
            }).ToList()
        );

        // Persist aggregate (single database operation, domain events dispatched)
        await _claimRepo.SaveAsync(claim);

        return Result.Success(new ClaimSubmissionResult
        {
            ClaimId = claim.Id.Value,
            ClaimNumber = claim.ClaimNumber.Value,
            Status = claim.Status.ToString()
        });
    }

    public async Task<Result<AdjudicationResult>> AdjudicateClaimAsync(AdjudicateClaimCommand command)
    {
        // Load aggregate
        var claim = await _claimRepo.GetByIdAsync(ClaimId.From(command.ClaimId));
        if (claim == null)
            return Result.Failure<AdjudicationResult>("Claim not found");

        // Get eligibility (ACL translates Member context)
        var eligibility = await _memberClient.GetEligibilityAsync(claim.MemberId, claim.ServiceDate);

        // Get credential (ACL translates Provider context)
        var credential = await _providerClient.GetCredentialAsync(claim.ProviderId, claim.ServiceDate);

        // Get pricing
        var pricing = await _feeScheduleRepo.GetForStateAsync(command.StateCode);

        // Adjudicate (business logic in domain model)
        var result = claim.Adjudicate(eligibility, credential, pricing, _authPolicy);

        // Persist (single database operation)
        await _claimRepo.SaveAsync(claim);

        return Result.Success(result);
    }
}

// 4. API CONTROLLER - Thin layer over application service

public class ClaimsController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IClaimApplicationService _claimService;

    [HttpPost("api/claims")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitClaim([FromBody] SubmitClaimCommand command)
    {
        var result = await _claimService.SubmitClaimAsync(command);

        if (result.IsSuccess)
        {
            return Ok(new
            {
                claimNumber = result.Value.ClaimNumber,
                claimId = result.Value.ClaimId,
                status = result.Value.Status,
                _links = new
                {
                    self = $"/api/claims/{result.Value.ClaimId}",
                    adjudicate = $"/api/claims/{result.Value.ClaimId}/adjudicate"
                }
            });
        }

        return BadRequest(new { error = result.Error });
    }

    [HttpPost("api/claims/{claimId}/adjudicate")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> AdjudicateClaim(Guid claimId)
    {
        var result = await _claimService.AdjudicateClaimAsync(new AdjudicateClaimCommand { ClaimId = claimId });

        if (result.IsSuccess)
        {
            return Ok(new
            {
                status = result.Value.Status.ToString(),
                approvedAmount = result.Value.Status == AdjudicationStatus.Approved
                    ? result.Value.ApprovedAmount
                    : null,
                denialReason = result.Value.Status == AdjudicationStatus.Denied
                    ? result.Value.DenialReason.ToString()
                    : null
            });
        }

        return BadRequest(new { error = result.Error });
    }
}
```

**Benefits Achieved:**

| Metric | Before (Technical Services) | After (Bounded Context) | Improvement |
|--------|----------------------------|------------------------|-------------|
| **Services Modified per Change** | Multiple services | 1 service | Single team ownership |
| **Deployment Frequency** | Every 5 weeks | Every 2 weeks | Reduced cycle time |
| **Change Failure Rate** | Elevated | Reduced | Fewer cross-service regressions |
| **Mean Time to Recovery** | Hours | ~45 minutes | Faster failure isolation |
| **Developer Cognitive Load** | 5+ services to understand | 1 bounded context | Focused scope |
| **Test Execution Time** | Extended | Shorter | Context-isolated testing |
| **Lines of Code per Feature** | Complex multi-service changes | Focused single-context changes | Reduced surface area |
| **Database Round-Trips** | 7+ per operation | 1-2 per operation | Aggregate boundary enforcement |

**Key Improvements:**

1. **Business Logic Encapsulation**: All claim adjudication logic in `Claim` aggregate, not scattered across 5 services
2. **Clear Ownership**: Claims team owns entire Claims Processing bounded context
3. **Rich Domain Model**: `Claim` has behaviors (`Adjudicate()`, `Submit()`) not just properties
4. **Ubiquitous Language**: Code uses domain terms (Adjudicate, Submit, Deny) understood by business experts
5. **Single Deployment Unit**: Change claims logic → deploy 1 service (not 3-5 services)
6. **Testability**: Test `Claim` aggregate without mocking 5 services
7. **Performance**: 1 database operation to save aggregate (vs 7+ round-trips in legacy)

